\begin{definition}
\label{def:3-16-extra-3}



For a smooth map $F:M\to N$, the global differential, or global tangent map,
is
\[
dF:TM\to TN,
\qquad dF|_{T_pM}=dF_p.
\]
Thus $dF(v)=dF_p(v)$ for $v\in T_pM$.
\end{definition}

